      "title": "Malta",
      "publisher": "Wikipedia",
      "author": null,
      "published_at": null,
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/?curid=19137",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-10-18T16:54:40.330Z",
      "sha256": "e149566c0ba13b721bd0aeb1707f672bc46e21695bc5e9a5db3c864713755adf",
      "rendered": false,
      "scraped": false,
      "excerpts": [
        "Malta, officially the Republic of Malta, is an island country located in the central Mediterranean Sea.",
        "It consists of a number of islands, of which Malta and Gozo are the two main ones—south of Italy, east of Tunisia, and north of Libya.",
        "Malta is the world's tenth-smallest country by area, ninth-most densely populated, and 166th most populated.",
        "It consists of a single urban region, because of which it is often described as a city-state.",
        "The two official languages are Maltese—recognised as the national language—and English.",
        "The island of Malta has been inhabited since at least 6500 BC, during the Mesolithic period.",
        "Its location at the centre of the Mediterranean has historically given it great geostrategic importance, with multiple powers having ruled the islands and shaped its culture and society.",
        "Included among these powers the Phoenicians, Carthaginians, Greeks, and Romans in antiquity; the Arabs, Normans, and Aragonese during the Middle Ages; and the Knights Hospitaller, French, and British in the modern era.",
        "Malta came under British rule as a crown colony in the early 19th century and served as the headquarters of the British Mediterranean Fleet.",
        "It was sieged by the Axis powers during World War II and was also an Allied base for its area.",
        "The country gained independence in 1964, and established its current parliamentary republic in 1974.",
        "It has been a member state of the Commonwealth of Nations and the United Nations since its independence, joining the European Union (EU) in 2004 and the eurozone monetary union in 2008."
      ]
